abstract: >-
  The Czech WordNet is a lexical database of Czech.  Nouns, verbs,
  adjectives and adverbs are grouped into sets of synonyms (synsets),
  each standing for one concept, and the synsets are linked by semantic
  relations such as hypernymy, meronymy and antonymy.  Almost all
  synsets are linked to Princeton WordNet and, through the Interlingual
  Index, to wordnets of other languages.  It was created by the Natural
  Language Processing Centre, Faculty of Informatics, Masaryk
  University, Brno, and is maintained and extended by the Computational
  Linguistics Lab at Palacký University, Olomouc.  It is released in
  WN-LMF, for use with the wn Python module.
